inal-word-the-hidden-history-of-human-rights-in-idaho/","line":46},{"title":"Kootenai County Task Force on Human Relations","target":"https://www.idahohumanrights.org/","line":46},{"title":"20 educational programs","target":"https://www.wassmuthcenter.org/about-the-anne-frank-memorial/#","line":56},{"title":"RIPL collective","target":"https://www.wassmuthcenter.org/ripl-collective/","line":58},{"title":"Jeff Westhoff","target":"https://idahocapitalsun.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Westhoff-Headshot-1891x2048.png","line":62,"embedded":true},{"title":"“Wassmuth Powerful Principles,”","target":"https://www.wassmuthcenter.org/powerful-practices/","line":66},{"title":"H-RISE Leadership Program","target":"https://www.wassmuthcenter.org/h-rise/","line":72},{"title":"Bill Wassmuth sign at the Wassmuth Center for Human Rights","target":"https://idahocapitalsun.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Wassmuth-sign.jpg","line":82,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Believing in the goodness of people: Idaho human rights center celebrates 30-year anniversary • Idaho Capital Sun","source":"https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/06/18/believing-in-the-goodness-of-people-idaho-human-rights-center-celebrates-30-year-anniversary/?utm_source=newsletters.idahocapitalsun.com&utm_medium=newsletter&utm_campaign=report-tax-cuts-benefit-rich-idahoans-wassmuth-center-celebrates-30-years-lawmakers-demand-info-on-trump-s-use-of-national-park-fees&_bhlid=b62a2ad552922d25482f71d52f18390ee30335cc","author":["[[Valentin Termite]]"],"published":"2026-06-18","created":"2026-07-08","description":"The Wassmuth Center for Human Rights, a staple of the Boise nonprofit scene, will celebrate its 30 year anniversary Saturday in commemoration of its community growth and impact. The event looks to celebrate this long history of human rights struggles, their complicated present and how the community, brought together under the umbrella of education, may re-center human rights in everyday life."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},